# .gcloudignore (repo root) -- ALLOWLIST. Everything is ignored, then only
# what the nerd-api image needs is let back in.
#
# Why an allowlist: the only Cloud Build submitted from the repo root is the
# nerd-api image (cloudbuild.api.yaml, via `scripts/deploy.sh candidate api`).
# The root holds local-only data that must never reach the Cloud Build
# source bucket: Firestore emulator exports (emulator-data/, which contains
# the seeded passwords document), .scratch/ working files, the frontend/lib
# JSON documents including passwords.json, .claude/, .env files, and the
# ncademi_archive. An exclusion list fails open whenever a new local file
# appears; an allowlist fails closed. When this file exists, gcloud does not
# read .gitignore.
#
# The entries below are exactly what Dockerfile.api COPYs, plus the two build
# files. If Dockerfile.api gains a COPY, add its source here, then check with:
#   gcloud meta list-files-for-upload --project edtech-agent-2026
*

!Dockerfile.api
!cloudbuild.api.yaml
!requirements.txt
!constraints.txt
!prompts/
!prompts/**
!nerd_core/
!nerd_core/**
!api/
!api/**
!templates/
!templates/**

# Re-exclude build residue inside the allowed directories.
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.DS_Store
